## 7. Best Practices

### Use `comptime_int` and `comptime_float` for Constants

Zig provides untyped arithmetic types for compile-time numbers:

```zig
const a: comptime_int = 1000;          // No runtime representation
const b = 1000;                        // Inferred as comptime_int
const c: u32 = 1000;                   // Forced to runtime type
```

Let the compiler keep constants in the highest precision until forced to materialize them.

### Prefer Comptime Parameters Over Runtime Parameters for Polymorphism

```zig
// GOOD - type information captured at compile time
fn process(comptime T: type, data: []T) void {
    // T is known, compiler can optimize
}

// BAD - type erased at runtime
fn processDyn(ptr: *anyopaque, size: usize, comptime T: type) void {
    // Avoid unless necessary for vtables
}
```

### Compose Comptime Functions Like Runtime Functions

Break down complex comptime logic into small, testable functions:

```zig
fn isPowerOfTwo(comptime x: comptime_int) bool {
    return x > 0 and (x & (x - 1)) == 0;
}

fn validatePowerOfTwo(comptime x: comptime_int) void {
    if (!isPowerOfTwo(x)) {
        @compileError(std.fmt.comptimePrint("{d} is not a power of two", .{x}));
    }
}

fn Buffer(comptime size: usize) type {
    validatePowerOfTwo(size);
    return [size]u8;
}
```

### Use `std.mem` and `std.fmt` Comptime Variants

The standard library provides comptime-friendly functions:

```zig
const suffix = comptime std.fmt.comptimePrint("_{d}", .{version});
const name = comptime "my_type" ++ suffix;  // String concatenation
```

Avoid runtime allocation in comptime when possible—use fixed buffers or comptime allocators.

### Document Comptime Requirements

When writing generic functions, explicitly state which parameters must be comptime-known:

```zig
/// Creates an array of type T with length L.
/// L must be known at compile time (array sizes require comptime).
/// T can be any type.
fn createArray(comptime T: type, comptime L: usize) [L]T {
    // ...
}
```

### Test Comptime Code with `comptime` Blocks in Tests

```zig
test "comptime string generation" {
    const result = comptime blk: {
        var buf: [32]u8 = undefined;
        const s = std.fmt.bufPrint(&buf, "{}", .{42}) catch unreachable;
        break :blk s;
    };
    try std.testing.expectEqualStrings("42", result);
}
```

